Title: each and eachSeries not passing back values to results array - why?
Description: This is probably my misunderstanding, but there's a small chance of a bug

``` javascript

async.each([1,2,3], function(value,cb){
    setTimeout(function(){
        cb(null,value);
    },200);

},function complete(err, results) {
    console.log(err,results);  //results is undefined here, err is null
});


async.eachSeries([1,2,3], function(value,cb){
    setTimeout(function(){
        cb(null,value);
    },200);

},function complete(err, results) {
    console.log(err,results); //results is undefined here, err is null as expected
});
```

for the async.series and async.parallel apis, we have the results argument being populated as an array, but with async.each and async.eachSeries, this does not seem to be the case.

is there something I am missing?

thanks!


